.\" kld.1 — manual for the kldload operator console hub. mdoc, OpenBSD
.\" section order. Keep in lockstep with the --help banner in main.go.
.Dd September 26, 2026
.Dt KLD 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kld
.Nd the kldload operator console, in a terminal
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar section Op Ar sub-tab
.Nm
.Fl -gui
.Op Ar section
.Nm
.Ar section
.Op Ar sub-tab
.Fl -print
.Nm
.Cm install
.Nm
.Fl -version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the kldload operator console as one program for a desktop and a headless
box alike:
Overview; Machines (VMs, snapshots, microVMs, appliances, factory,
networks, pools);
Storage (pools, topology, datasets, snapshots, boot environments, ARC);
Network (planes, peers, enrolled, fleet, check);
Cluster (nodes, pods, deployments, services, events, logs, describe);
Ansible (hosts, groups, plays); Helm (releases, examples);
Metrics (host, storage, machines, mesh, targets: Prometheus, as sparklines);
Estate (drift, units, events); and Provision (armed, feed, goldens,
answers).
It is a terminal program, the default everywhere, with the ten sections
of the web console, each with sub-tabs;
.Fl -gui
opens this same console in a terminal window through
.Xr kldload-term 1 :
the GUI is the TUI, so nothing drifts between them.
The sections:
Overview, Machines, Storage, Network, Cluster, Metrics, Estate and Provision.
Each section is read from the tool that owns the fact and shown as it is:
.Xr kldload-estate 8
for the machines and the drift,
.Xr kldload-doctor 8
for the host's health,
.Xr zpool 8
and
.Xr kldload-rollback 8
for storage and boot environments,
.Xr wg 8
for the mesh,
.Xr kubectl 1
for the cluster after a port probe of the apiserver, the Prometheus targets
API for metrics, and
.Xr kldload-netboot-server 8
for the rack.
.Pp
.Nm
is a hub, not another console.
The deep views stay in
.Xr vmxplore 1 ,
.Xr zxplore 1 ,
.Xr wgx 1
and
.Xr k9s 1 ;
.Nm
opens the one that belongs to the current section on
.Ic Enter
and returns when it exits.
Its verbs run the shipped commands
.Xr kvm-clone 8 ,
.Xr kvm-snap 8
and
.Xr kvm-delete 8 ,
never a re-implementation of them, so what the terminal does is what the
estate tests prove.
.Pp
With a
.Ar section
argument the console opens on that section.
With
.Fl -print
it renders that section once to standard output, without a terminal, and
exits; the text is the same the console shows.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ar section
One of
.Cm overview , machines , storage , network , cluster , metrics , estate
or
.Cm provision ,
case-insensitive.
.It Fl -gui
This console in a terminal window; needs a display.
.It Fl -print
Render the named section once and exit.
Useful from scripts and over an ssh command that has no terminal.
.It Fl -version
Print the version and the build stamp.
.It Fl h , -help
Print the usage and the key map, and exit 0.
.El
.Sh THE INSTALL MENU
.Nm Cm install
is the live medium's front door and the netboot menu's twin: it asks the
profile, the distribution (marked offline when this medium carries its
mirror), the security posture (standard, encrypted, Secure Boot, both),
the disk (zvols, zram and the medium's own disk are left out), the
hostname, the admin user and password, and a passphrase when encrypting,
shows a summary, writes the same answers file the netboot menu writes
(mode 0600 under /run/kldload) and hands it to
.Xr kldload-install-target 8
.Fl -config .
Its other entries open the Provision section to arm another machine,
the operator console, or a shell.
.Ev KLD_INSTALL_DRYRUN Ns =1
writes the file and stops.
.Sh KEYS
.Bl -tag -width "Shift-Tab" -compact
.It Ic 1 No to Ic 9 , Ic 0
Switch to that section
.Pq Ic h No and Ic l No step through them .
.It Ic Tab , Shift-Tab
Next and previous sub-tab of the section
.Pq also Ic \&[ No and Ic \&] .
.It Ic j , k
Move the selection down and up;
.Ic g
and
.Ic G
first and last;
.Ic ctrl+f
and
.Ic ctrl+b
a page.
.It Ic Space
Mark the row; a verb then runs on every marked row of the tab, in order,
and reports how many succeeded and which failed
.Pq Ic ctrl+a No marks or clears them all .
.It Ic Enter
Drill in: a VM's snapshots, a dataset's snapshots, a group's hosts.
.It Ic Esc
Leave a drill-in.
.It Ic /
Filter the rows; Enter keeps the filter, Esc clears it.
.It Ic o
Sort by the next column, then descending, then the tool's own order.
.It Ic i
Show or hide the detail pane.
.It Ic r
Reload the sub-tab.
.It Ic \&?
The keys, including every verb of the current sub-tab.
.It Ic q
Quit.
.El
.Pp
Verbs act on the selected row and run the shipped command for it; the
detail pane shows the exact command each key would run.
A destructive verb asks for the row's name to be typed back and does
nothing otherwise; a verb that needs more asks for it on the status line.
Verbs that take the terminal (a serial console, ssh, pod logs and shells,
plays, helm installs) return to
.Nm
when they exit.
The verbs, by sub-tab:
.Bl -tag -width "Storage / Boot envs" -compact
